My first take-away is: _winit_ is trying to release a display that is not there anymore.
This can be fixed by either not trying to make it do that, or by making it resilient to this misuse.

This diff does the second approach and prevents the crash:

```diff
diff --git a/src/platform_impl/macos/window_delegate.rs b/src/platform_impl/macos/window_delegate.rs
index 1e3675f1..3375f67f 100644
--- a/src/platform_impl/macos/window_delegate.rs
+++ b/src/platform_impl/macos/window_delegate.rs
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ use objc2_foundation::{
     NSObject, NSObjectNSDelayedPerforming, NSObjectNSThreadPerformAdditions, NSObjectProtocol,
     NSPoint, NSRect, NSSize, NSString,
 };
+use tracing::warn;
 
 use super::app_state::ApplicationDelegate;
 use super::cursor::cursor_from_icon; 
@@ -1390,13 +1394,20 @@ impl WindowDelegate {
                 toggle_fullscreen(self.window());
             },
             (Some(Fullscreen::Exclusive(ref video_mode)), None) => {
-                unsafe {
-                    ffi::CGRestorePermanentDisplayConfiguration();
-                    assert_eq!(
-                        ffi::CGDisplayRelease(video_mode.monitor().native_identifier()),
-                        ffi::kCGErrorSuccess
-                    );
-                };
+                let monitor = video_mode.monitor();
+                let available_monitors = monitor::available_monitors();
+                if available_monitors.contains(&monitor) {
+                    unsafe {
+                        ffi::CGRestorePermanentDisplayConfiguration();
+                        assert_eq!(
+                            ffi::CGDisplayRelease(monitor.native_identifier()),
+                            ffi::kCGErrorSuccess
+                        );
+                    };
+                } else {
+                    warn!(monitor=monitor.name(), "Tried to restore exclusive fullscreen on a monitor that is no longer available");
+                }
+
                 toggle_fullscreen(self.window());
             },
             (Some(Fullscreen::Borderless(_)), Some(Fullscreen::Exclusive(_))) => {
```

Opened as PR on winit as well: https://github.com/rust-windowing/winit/pull/3733

I don't think it's a good change necessarily, because it is at best a bandaid. The better solution would be to ensure that we only try to operate on screens that are still available at all times, but I'm not sure how to do that in another way.

